  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">for support of feminist-led abortion rights movements in West and Central Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This renewal grant to the Global Fund for Women (GFW) will support the youth-led movement for abortion rights in Benin, Cameroon, C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire, and Guinea. GFW and a regional Movement Committee seek to expand access to safe abortion, especially for marginalized groups, by strengthening interconnections between abortion rights, sexual and reproductive justice, and gender justice activism. During the grant period, the Movement Committee and GFW will deepen participatory grantmaking, capacity strengthening, and collective action with the regional abortion rights ecosystem. In addition, GFW and its partners seek to influence philanthropic practice in feminist, movement-led grantmaking and governance. (Strategy: Global Reproductive Equity)</narrative>
  </description>
